# Scene

metatrom-ag/.github#37, sub-issue of metatrom-ag/claude-code-plugins#281 (step 10 of #259): the estimate reads the files the work goes through from a field the author fills on purpose. Run 7 (#278) showed the estimate's input is the limit — paths named in passing predict nothing (ρ 0.07 over 340 issues). Built by a Claude subagent in a scratch clone, on the branch feat/37-goes-through from origin/main after #36 merged.

# Decided

- Field id `goes-through`, label *Goes through*, type textarea, in all three templates: `1-idea.yml`, `2-bug.yml`, `3-action.yml`.
- Placed directly above the *Story Points* dropdown, so the author names the paths before they pick a size.
- Required in Bug and Action, optional in Idea — an idea's author may not yet know the code; a bug's or action's does.
- Description in one sentence: the files or folders the work changes as far as known, one per line, a file where known, else its folder; the estimate counts from it. Placeholder shows one file and one folder (`src/orders/total.ts`, `docs/`).
- The YAML was checked by parsing all three files (Ruby's YAML, no node parser installed) and asserting `goes-through` sits at the index before `story-points` with the right `required`.
- The commit's author was reset before push: the scratch clone had no local identity and git fell back to a hostname email; the identity now matches the main checkout.

